    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1091">

                <pb facs="1331" n="1313" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg1313"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">831.24/3–1446</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Venezuela</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-14T21:00:00-05:00">March 14, 1946—9 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>131. Dept. has notified Venezuelan representatives of availability for their
                    purchase from surplus of military ground equipment for 1 Battalion of Infantry,
                    1 Battery of Light Field Artillery, 2,000 .45 calibre pistols for police
                    purposes, and the following aircraft: 3 C–47’s,5 (C–45’s, AT–11’s, or
                    AT–7’s).</p>
                <pb facs="1332" n="1314" xml:id="pg1314"/>
                <p>Details concerning prices and terms to be arranged by Venezuelan representatives
                    directly with Foreign Liquidation Commission.</p>
                <p>Above equipment excludes some civilian items, particularly motor vehicles, not
                    now available in surplus.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
